; 15-understand-why-a-step-succeeded.kurt
;
; Understand why a step succeeded
;
; Kurt prints a short reason beside every accepted formula. Labels replace raw source locations
; when available. For more detail, use `cert` after a step:

bool A, B
use A implies B  "modus-ponens"
use A
B
cert 11

; The certificate of line 11 shows:
;
; - the goal (`B`),
; - the rule or fact used (`A implies B`, line 9, with its label "modus-ponens"),
; - how the rule is read (premise ⇒ conclusion),
; - the premises and their lines (`A`, line 10), and
; - the kernel's verdict (checked).
;
; A rule with variables also shows how they were instantiated. `cert` without a line number shows
; the most recent line with a certificate.
